---
/**
 * How ScreenTrail handles data, for an MSP's security lead. Every statement here is held to the
 * repository (docs/STATUS.md, docs/security/*, the build guide's invariants) as of 2026-11-18, and the
 * limits are stated as plainly as the protections.
 *
 * The page opens on a map of the PC's edge: what stays on the technician's PC, what crosses it, and
 * the local-only switch that cuts the drafting route. The switch is a plain checkbox styled with :has(),
 * so it works without script under the site's CSP.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import '../styles/security.css';

const docs = `${site.repo}/tree/main/docs/security`;
const blob = `${site.repo}/blob/main/docs/security`;
---
<Base title="Security and privacy" description="How ScreenTrail captures, masks, stores and sends session data, what it does not protect against yet, and how to report a vulnerability.">
  <div class="page wrap sec">
    <header class="page-head sec-head">
      <h1>What ScreenTrail captures, and what it does with it.</h1>
      <p class="sub">Written for the security review your clients will ask for. Where something is not built or not measured yet, this page says so.</p>
      <p class="sec-status" role="note">
        <span class="sec-chip">Not released</span>
        <span><strong>ScreenTrail is in development.</strong> Nothing here is ready for production use or customer data outside a pilot agreement. The pilot is where the protections below are checked on real sessions.</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="edge" aria-labelledby="edge-cap">
      <input class="edge-switch" type="checkbox" id="local-only" aria-describedby="edge-cap" />
      <div class="edge-bar">
        <p id="edge-cap" class="edge-cap">Where session data goes. Switch on local-only mode to see the drafting route cut.</p>
        <label class="edge-toggle" for="local-only">
          <span class="edge-knob" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>Local-only mode</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="edge-map">
        <section class="zone zone-pc" aria-labelledby="z-pc">
          <p id="z-pc" class="zone-name">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2.5" y="3.5" width="15" height="10" rx="1.5"/><path d="M7 17h6M10 13.5V17"/></svg>
            On the technician's PC
          </p>
          <ol class="lane">
            <li><b>Screen</b><span>Remote-tool windows only</span></li>
            <li class="is-mask"><b>Masked</b><span>Text read in memory, secrets painted out</span></li>
            <li><b>Encrypted store</b><span>Deleted after 7 days by default</span></li>
          </ol>
          <ol class="lane">
            <li><b>Microphone</b><span>The technician's own</span></li>
            <li><b>Transcribed</b><span>Speech to text on the PC</span></li>
            <li class="is-stay"><b>Raw audio</b><span>Never leaves the PC</span></li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <div class="edge-line" aria-hidden="true"><span>the PC's edge</span></div>

        <section class="zone zone-out" aria-labelledby="z-out">
          <p id="z-out" class="zone-name">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h11M11 6l4 4-4 4"/></svg>
            What leaves it
          </p>
          <div class="route route-draft">
            <p class="route-when">For drafting</p>
            <p class="route-what">Masked screenshots, the click and window timeline, the technician's words</p>
            <p class="route-to">ScreenTrail backend, then Gemini or Claude, as the MSP chooses</p>
            <p class="route-off">Local-only mode: nothing is sent for drafting</p>
          </div>
          <div class="route route-pub">
            <p class="route-when">On Publish</p>
            <p class="route-what">Only what the technician approved</p>
            <p class="route-to">The note and time entry to the ConnectWise ticket, the article to Hudu</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="with-toc sec-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <section aria-labelledby="when-it-captures">
        <h2 id="when-it-captures">When it captures</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2.5" y="4" width="15" height="11" rx="1.5"/><path d="M2.5 7h15"/></svg>
            <p>Only while a remote-support tool (ScreenConnect, Remote Desktop, Splashtop, TeamViewer, AnyDesk) is the window in front, or when the technician starts a session by hand.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5.5h12M4 10h12M4 14.5h7"/></svg>
            <p>Only that tool's windows, plus admin tools such as PowerShell, Event Viewer or Services if the MSP allows them. Capturing every window is off unless turned on and confirmed.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="7" width="14" height="6" rx="3"/><circle cx="6.5" cy="10" r="1.3" class="rec"/></svg>
            <p>A recording pill is on screen for the whole session. If the app showing it stops responding, the capture service stops capturing within seconds.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="9" width="12" height="8" rx="1.5"/><path d="M7 9V6.5a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V9"/></svg>
            <p>Capture pauses while a password field has focus, and apps on the exclusion list are not captured.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="what-is-masked-and-where">
        <h2 id="what-is-masked-and-where">What is masked, and where</h2>
        <p>Each screenshot waits in memory on the technician's PC while its text is read (OCR, on the PC). Passwords, card numbers, keys and similar values that are found are painted out of the image before it is written to disk or sent anywhere. A frame that cannot be read in time is dropped and counted, not stored unmasked.</p>

        <figure class="measure" aria-labelledby="measure-cap">
          <figcaption id="measure-cap">
            <strong>This is not a guarantee.</strong> Masking depends on the text being read correctly. Secrets masked whole, on synthetic test pages:
          </figcaption>
          <dl class="bars">
            <div class="bar bar-97">
              <dt>At normal display scaling</dt>
              <dd><span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill"></span><span class="bar-goal"></span></span><span class="bar-num">97%</span></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="bar bar-83">
              <dt>Through a scaled, compressed remote viewer</dt>
              <dd><span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill"></span><span class="bar-goal"></span></span><span class="bar-num">83%</span></dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="measure-key"><span class="key-goal" aria-hidden="true"></span>Target before release: 98% on real, labelled sessions, measured in the pilot.</p>
        </figure>

        <p>The cases the rules do not yet cover are listed in the <a href={`${blob}/data-flow.md`}>data-flow document</a>. Every draft says how many items were masked so the technician can check them before publishing.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="voice">
        <h2 id="voice">Voice</h2>
        <p>Only the technician's own microphone is used, and speech is transcribed on the PC. The end user's voice is not recorded.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="what-leaves-the-pc">
        <h2 id="what-leaves-the-pc">What leaves the PC</h2>
        <table class="facts routes">
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">For drafting</th><td>The masked screenshots, the click and window timeline, and the technician's transcribed words go to the ScreenTrail backend, which asks the drafting model (Gemini or Claude, as the MSP chooses) for the note. Raw audio never leaves the PC.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">On publish</th><td>Only what the technician approved: the note and time entry to the ConnectWise ticket, the article to Hudu. Nothing is published without the technician pressing Publish.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Local-only mode</th><td>Nothing is sent for drafting. The only traffic left is the publish the technician asks for and the policy check. Your ScreenTrail owner can lock it on for every technician.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="storage">
        <h2 id="storage">Storage</h2>
        <dl class="store">
          <div><dt>Sessions</dt><dd>Kept in an encrypted database on the PC, keyed to the Windows account.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Credentials</dt><dd>PSA and documentation credentials are held by the backend in an encrypted vault, and only your ScreenTrail owner can add or change them, in the web admin.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Captures</dt><dd>Screenshots and audio are deleted after the retention period the MSP sets (seven days by default). Discarding a session deletes its captures.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Logs</dt><dd>Record what happened, never what was on screen or said.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="gaps" aria-labelledby="what-is-not-protected-yet">
        <h2 id="what-is-not-protected-yet">What is not protected yet</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Masking misses some values: an unlabelled run of only one kind of character, mirrored layouts, and text split across rows at some display scales.</li>
          <li>Some window effects in remote tools can let a few pixels of what is behind them into a screenshot. Capturing single windows is the full fix and is planned.</li>
          <li>The ConnectWise and Hudu connections have been tested against recorded responses, not live accounts yet.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The full list, with reasons, is in the <a href={`${blob}/threat-model.md`}>threat model</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="the-privacy-pack">
        <h2 id="the-privacy-pack">The privacy pack</h2>
        <p>The data-flow description, threat model, security questionnaire answers and consent guidance are public in the repository's security folder. They have not yet been reviewed by an outside security lead, and say so.</p>
        <ul class="files">
          <li><a href={`${blob}/data-flow.md`}><span class="file-name">data-flow.md</span><span>What is captured, masked, stored and sent</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={`${blob}/threat-model.md`}><span class="file-name">threat-model.md</span><span>What it protects against, and what not yet</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={docs}><span class="file-name">docs/security/</span><span>The whole folder, questionnaire answers included</span></a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="report" aria-labelledby="report">
        <h2 id="report">Report a vulnerability</h2>
        <div class="mail">
          <p class="mail-row"><span>To</span><a href={`mailto:${site.securityEmail}`}>{site.securityEmail}</a></p>
          <p class="mail-row"><span>Include</span>What you found and how to reproduce it</p>
          <p class="mail-row"><span>Answer</span>Within three working days</p>
        </div>
        <p>Please give us a reasonable time to fix it before telling anyone else, and do not access data that is not yours or degrade the service while testing. We will keep you told of progress, and credit you if you want to be named. Our <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> has the same details.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="h-toc">
      <h2 id="h-toc">On this page</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#when-it-captures">When it captures</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-is-masked-and-where">What is masked, and where</a></li>
        <li><a href="#voice">Voice</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-leaves-the-pc">What leaves the PC</a></li>
        <li><a href="#storage">Storage</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-is-not-protected-yet">What is not protected yet</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-privacy-pack">The privacy pack</a></li>
        <li><a href="#report">Report a vulnerability</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
